.TH RANDOM 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Random \- pseudo-random number generation
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Random
module uses a Mersenne Twister (std::mt19937) seeded from std::random_device.
The generator is shared (static) across all calls within one process run.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS RandFloat
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
float() RandFloat()
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns a uniformly distributed random float in [0.0, 1.0).
.SS RandChoice
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
any() RandChoice(container: list()|tuple()|string()|set()|range())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns a randomly selected element from container.
Supported: list, tuple, string (returns single-char string), set, range.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBTypeError\fR, \fBEmptyContainerError\fR
.SS Shuffle
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
list()|tuple()|string() Shuffle(container)
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns a new shuffled copy of container (list, tuple, or string).
Sets and ranges raise \fBTypeError\fR.
Original is NOT mutated.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBTypeError\fR
.SS Sample
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
list()|tuple()|set()|string() Sample(container, k: int())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns k unique randomly selected deep-copy elements from container,
additionally shuffled.
Supported: list, tuple, set, range, string.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBTypeError\fR, \fBValueError\fR (k out of range)
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Math(3)
